  "kind": "statement",
  "title": "Properness is local on the target",
  "statement": "Let $f\\colon Y\\to X$ be a morphism. If $X$ has an open cover\n$(V_i)$ such that every $f^{-1}(V_i)\\to V_i$ is proper, then $f$ is\nproper.",
  "source": {
    "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-nagata-compactification/sk-lem-nagata-sketch-blowups/lemma-nagata-projective-target-local.md",
    "place": "node lemma-nagata-projective-target-local, order 88",
    "external": [
      {
        "document": "Stacks Project",
        "place": "Tag 08J0"
      }
    ]
  },
  "stmt_deps": [],
  "proof": [
    {
      "text": "Properness is a Zariski-local property on the target. Apply the verified\ntarget-locality instance\n`AlgebraicGeometry.IsProper.instIsZariskiLocalAtTarget` to the open\ncover $(V_i)$; its local hypotheses are exactly the properness hypotheses in\nthe statement, and it returns that $f$ is proper.",
      "uses": [],
      "elementary": null
    },
    {
      "text": "*Warning.* The analogous assertion with ``projective'' in place of\n``proper'' is false for the finite-projective-space definition used here;\nsee Stacks Project Tag 08J0. No projectivity conclusion is used below.",
      "uses": [],
      "elementary": null
    }
  ],
